      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Report of an acute inflammatory syndrome of the right side of the belly with fever, polyleucocytosis and diabetes in a 35 years old patient with chronic calcified pancreatitis. The right colon was moved forward by an important retroperitoneal infiltration and the pathology demonstrated a cytosteatonecrosis. The post-operative period was disturbed by hyperamylasemia, hyperamylasuria and an external pancreatic fistule."},
